# Generated documents, by the exact names SPEC 3.6 uses in its examples.
#
# `audio:script` and `kssr:review` print to stdout and save nothing, because a
# committed copy drifts from the pack on the first content edit and a stale
# review form is worse than none — it looks current. Redirecting one to a file
# is still the way you get something to hand to a person, and one of those files
# then sits in the root waiting for the next `git add -A`. It has already been
# committed once.
#
# Exact names, not `/*.md`. Ignoring every root markdown file would silently
# swallow the next CLAUDE.md-sized document somebody adds here, and a file git
# refuses to see fails quietly — which is the failure mode this repo keeps
# paying for. Redirect somewhere else and the pattern does not cover you; that
# is the trade, and it is the safer half of it.
/semakan-guru.md
/skrip-rakaman.md
